WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.430
<i>All right.
We're ready when you are.</i>


00:00:41.599 --> 00:00:43.369
<i>Should I cover my hair?</i>


00:00:44.001 --> 00:00:45.442
<i>What do you think?</i>


00:00:45.471 --> 00:00:48.540
<i>Ah, it's not gonna
make a difference to them,</i>


00:00:48.573 --> 00:00:51.813
<i>and it'll probably just
alienate people over here.</i>


00:00:51.842 --> 00:00:54.212
Now? You ready?


00:00:58.181 --> 00:00:59.922
My name is Helen Sterling


00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:03.959
and my son Andrew Sterling
is a journalist.


00:01:05.188 --> 00:01:07.158
I am not supposed to
be saying this to you


00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.089
but I have money for you.


00:01:09.124 --> 00:01:12.054
I'm in the process
of transferring to you


00:01:12.094 --> 00:01:14.025
everything I have in the world.


00:01:14.731 --> 00:01:15.970
I'm begging you.


00:01:17.032 --> 00:01:18.192
I'm sorry.


00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:20.664
-Oh, no.
-No, no, no, you're fine.


00:01:21.903 --> 00:01:24.002
Just, just be yourself.


00:01:24.038 --> 00:01:26.508
Myself doesn't make videos.


00:01:26.541 --> 00:01:28.353
You know what,
the eye line is off anyway.


00:01:28.377 --> 00:01:30.896
-Let's pretend these are right
underneath you. -


00:04:05.289 --> 00:04:07.259
All right,
you'll feel some tickles now.


00:04:08.591 --> 00:04:09.761
A little cold.


00:04:19.768 --> 00:04:23.647
<i>Hi, you've reached the assistant
special agent in-charge Eric Walsh.</i>


00:04:23.671 --> 00:04:28.411
<i>Please leave a message. If it's an
emergency, please dial 0 for assistance.</i>


00:04:28.443 --> 00:04:30.283
<i>Agent Walsh,
this is Helen Sterling.</i>


00:04:30.312 --> 00:04:33.612
<i>I wanted to follow up because
I haven't heard from you in,</i>


00:04:33.648 --> 00:04:36.817
<i>I don't know, I guess,
it's been a week now.</i>


00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:39.120
<i> Sorry, I missed your call.
My phone was charging.</i>


00:04:39.152 --> 00:04:40.792
<i>I have it with me now.</i>


00:04:40.821 --> 00:04:42.998
<i> Could you call me back, whenever?
It doesn't matter what time.</i>


00:04:43.022 --> 00:04:44.593
<i>It's Helen Sterling.</i>


00:04:44.624 --> 00:04:46.564
<i> Um, it keeps
going to voicemail,</i>


00:04:46.593 --> 00:04:48.493
<i> so I guess you're
out of the office today.</i>


00:04:48.529 --> 00:04:51.228
<i> If you check this,
will you please let me know?</i>


00:04:51.264 --> 00:04:53.334
<i> I tried dialing 0, by
the way, but the operator</i>


00:04:53.366 --> 00:04:56.865
<i> didn't know who
to transfer me to, so...</i>


00:04:56.902 --> 00:04:59.173
<i> Okay, just,
will you call me back?</i>


00:05:10.048 --> 00:05:12.178
Good evening, Millie!


00:05:12.918 --> 00:05:15.548
I've got your antibiotic
for you.


00:05:18.789 --> 00:05:20.159
Here you go.


00:05:21.725 --> 00:05:23.195
That's good.


00:05:25.996 --> 00:05:27.266
Hey.


00:05:27.298 --> 00:05:29.418
Can you finish up in here
and meet me outside, please?


00:05:29.666 --> 00:05:30.696
Mmm-hmm.


00:05:31.201 --> 00:05:32.301
What's up?


00:05:32.335 --> 00:05:34.205
-You have a visitor.
- Me?


00:05:34.237 --> 00:05:36.637
Yeah, a young woman,
Sheila, I think.


00:05:37.039 --> 00:05:38.578
Sheila.


00:05:38.607 --> 00:05:41.248
You know it's not a good time
to have personal visits, Helen.


00:05:41.278 --> 00:05:42.748
She's in 438.


00:05:43.879 --> 00:05:45.078
I'll see what she wants.


00:05:45.113 --> 00:05:47.292
Make it quick. You know we're
in the middle of an audit.


00:05:47.316 --> 00:05:48.516
<i>Right, boss.</i>


00:05:57.292 --> 00:05:58.451
Merry Christmas!


00:05:58.492 --> 00:06:00.462
You sounded terrible in there!


00:06:00.494 --> 00:06:04.564
Do not eat sushi
in Lebanon, trust me.


00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:06.768
How long has it been this way?


00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:10.140
It started, like,
that last week I was there,


00:06:10.171 --> 00:06:12.600
so like, I don't know,
two weeks.


00:06:12.639 --> 00:06:15.349
And of course you don't
have any kind of insurance?


00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:17.615
Welcome to
the freelance economy.


00:06:17.644 --> 00:06:18.814
Yeah. Lie down.


00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:20.044
Okay.


00:06:20.078 --> 00:06:21.648
Andy and I could both
win Pulitzers


00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.281
and still not make enough money
to even have to file taxes.


00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:28.087
Well, I offered to pay
Andy's insurance.


00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.490
But oh, no.
He's too stubborn.


00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:32.656
Too short-sighted.


00:06:32.691 --> 00:06:36.161
Well, I finally heard back from
my friend at the Red Cross.


00:06:36.194 --> 00:06:37.264
No luck there.


00:06:37.295 --> 00:06:38.965
But there is someone else.


00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:40.841
Yeah, well, let's not talk
about this now, okay?


00:06:40.865 --> 00:06:42.435
Helen, I'm worried.


00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:44.637
I feel like you
keeping this all quiet


00:06:44.669 --> 00:06:47.368
is just making it harder on you.


00:06:47.404 --> 00:06:49.974
It's kinda making it
harder on all of us.


00:06:50.908 --> 00:06:52.538
Sorry, I'll be right back.


00:06:54.077 --> 00:06:55.377
Oh, shit!


00:07:00.683 --> 00:07:01.883
- Hey.
- Hey.


00:07:20.103 --> 00:07:21.672
Here, this is for you.


00:07:21.703 --> 00:07:25.443
Take these now, and then
two a day for ten days.


00:07:25.907 --> 00:07:27.737
And next time,


00:07:27.776 --> 00:07:30.675
if there is a next time,
don't just show up.


00:07:30.711 --> 00:07:31.651
Call me first.


00:07:31.678 --> 00:07:33.549
I'm not getting you
in trouble, am I?


00:07:34.882 --> 00:07:35.982
I can handle it.


00:07:39.386 --> 00:07:40.897
So who was the person
that you were saying,


00:07:40.921 --> 00:07:42.960
-not the Red Cross, but somebody?
- Yeah.


00:07:42.988 --> 00:07:46.499
I was finally able to get the
number of Leo Spencer's mother.


00:07:47.628 --> 00:07:50.667
She's not the easiest person
to talk to, but...


00:07:52.065 --> 00:07:53.425
Please call her.


00:07:53.466 --> 00:07:56.495
I know they told you
that you can't tell anyone.


00:07:56.534 --> 00:07:58.004
But Charlotte can help.


00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.140
I'll think about it.


00:08:00.172 --> 00:08:02.532
Leo is part of that same club
that Andy and I are in.


00:08:02.574 --> 00:08:05.004
So we helped Charlotte
when Leo was in trouble.


00:08:05.043 --> 00:08:06.573
Andy never mentioned a club.


00:08:06.612 --> 00:08:08.872
It's a really amazing
group of people.


00:08:08.914 --> 00:08:11.483
So everyone pools their
resources together online.


00:08:11.515 --> 00:08:13.885
So you know where's safe
to go, where to eat,


00:08:13.918 --> 00:08:15.959
contacts, translators,
stuff like that.


00:08:15.987 --> 00:08:17.886
It's called the Viper Club.


00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:20.800
"The Viper Club"?


00:08:20.825 --> 00:08:22.255
Yeah, well...


00:08:22.292 --> 00:08:24.291
I didn't come up with the name.


00:08:24.327 --> 00:08:26.467
Can I just stay here for like...


00:08:26.495 --> 00:08:28.295
- Ten minutes.
- Okay.


00:09:19.912 --> 00:09:20.952
Yeah!


00:10:07.757 --> 00:10:08.587
What's up?


00:10:08.624 --> 00:10:09.824
Can you cover for me?


00:10:09.859 --> 00:10:11.229
I thought I could power through,


00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:14.129
but I'm burnt out. This is
my third double this week.


00:10:14.162 --> 00:10:15.422
Helen...


00:10:15.463 --> 00:10:16.763
I know, I know, I know.


00:10:16.798 --> 00:10:19.198
But I took Carmelyn's
because it was her birthday...


00:10:19.234 --> 00:10:20.563
Hmm.


00:10:26.108 --> 00:10:28.177
-I'll cover for you.
- Thank you.


00:10:28.209 --> 00:10:30.619
- Can you please get some rest?
- Yes.


00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:49.891
Wait!


00:11:19.156 --> 00:11:20.926
Step on the yellow line.


00:11:38.573 --> 00:11:42.083
<i>What brings you all the
way down to the city, Miss Sterling?</i>


00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:44.049
They sent me an e-mail.


00:11:44.078 --> 00:11:47.779
Fantastic, they finally
wrote to you directly.


00:11:47.816 --> 00:11:49.860
We have to pass this along
to our Intelligence Analysts...


00:11:49.884 --> 00:11:51.794
But we'll respond to it today.


00:11:51.819 --> 00:11:53.064
I understand
your sense of urgency,


00:11:53.088 --> 00:11:54.588
but this is not
going to happen today.


00:11:54.623 --> 00:11:56.523
No, it's going to happen today.


00:11:56.557 --> 00:11:58.186
I mean, my...


00:11:58.725 --> 00:11:59.856
They reached out,


00:11:59.894 --> 00:12:01.334
that means my son's still alive.


00:12:01.362 --> 00:12:04.431
It's not up to me. There's a
protocol we have to follow.


00:12:04.464 --> 00:12:06.594
An internal report
has to be generated.


00:12:06.633 --> 00:12:07.943
What does that mean?


00:12:08.201 --> 00:12:09.041
Helen,


00:12:09.069 --> 00:12:11.368
there are
a lot of people involved.


00:12:11.404 --> 00:12:13.465
And of course, we need access


00:12:13.507 --> 00:12:15.307
-to your e-mail accounts...
- Oh, sure.


00:12:15.342 --> 00:12:18.381
So we can see where the e-mail
might have been sent from.


00:12:18.411 --> 00:12:20.881
Okay. And, um, I took off
from work today


00:12:20.913 --> 00:12:23.843
so I can help you with this.


00:12:23.883 --> 00:12:24.842
I'm sorry.


00:12:24.883 --> 00:12:26.243
Nobody asked you to do that.


00:12:27.118 --> 00:12:28.759
Nobody "asked" me?


00:12:29.621 --> 00:12:31.730
Nobody asked me...


00:12:31.756 --> 00:12:33.556
-This is my child.
- I know this is upsetting,


00:12:33.591 --> 00:12:35.661
but we don't know
who we're dealing with yet.


00:12:35.694 --> 00:12:36.794
Even the State Department


00:12:36.828 --> 00:12:38.597
is struggling
to get information,


00:12:38.629 --> 00:12:40.299
and they already have
people over there.


00:12:40.331 --> 00:12:41.462
This is a delicate process.


00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:42.940
We don't have time for delicate.


00:12:42.967 --> 00:12:44.867
We're going to get Andy
home, Helen.


00:12:44.903 --> 00:12:46.702
You just have to trust
the process.


00:12:46.737 --> 00:12:49.977
I'm not leaving here
until we respond.


00:12:54.144 --> 00:12:56.145
Let me see what's possible.


00:13:18.967 --> 00:13:21.306
Can I have a water, please?


00:13:30.645 --> 00:13:32.815
I'm fine. What did he say?


00:13:35.949 --> 00:13:38.820
I'm going to forward you
a recommended response


00:13:38.853 --> 00:13:40.752
which you will put
into your own words.


00:13:40.786 --> 00:13:42.696
Send it to me.
We'll approve it


00:13:42.722 --> 00:13:44.292
and then you send it to them.


00:13:44.324 --> 00:13:45.324
When?


00:13:45.925 --> 00:13:47.024
Soon.


00:13:47.059 --> 00:13:48.629
How soon?


00:13:48.661 --> 00:13:51.702
We need to control
the pace of communication.


00:13:51.731 --> 00:13:53.361
Now, this might sound
counter-intuitive,


00:13:53.399 --> 00:13:57.198
but in our experience
with terrorist organizations,


00:13:57.236 --> 00:14:00.835
we've found that it's best
to take things slowly.


00:14:02.006 --> 00:14:04.006
You haven't told anybody, right?


00:14:05.911 --> 00:14:07.181
No.


00:14:07.212 --> 00:14:09.381
<i>Good. Keep it that way.</i>


00:14:10.781 --> 00:14:12.381
<i>One more thing.</i>


00:14:12.416 --> 00:14:14.645
<i>Money cannot exchange hands.</i>


00:14:15.718 --> 00:14:16.748
<i>That's illegal.</i>


00:14:16.787 --> 00:14:18.117
<i>What?</i>


00:14:20.024 --> 00:14:23.063
<i>Well, how do we get him back then?
What's the plan?</i>


00:14:23.093 --> 00:14:24.370
<i>I know this is hard,</i>


00:14:24.394 --> 00:14:25.738
<i> but we're going to
take it one step at a time.</i>


00:14:25.762 --> 00:14:28.032
<i>You didn't answer me.</i>


00:14:28.064 --> 00:14:31.893
<i>I promise you,
this is our top priority.</i>


00:14:50.051 --> 00:14:52.661
<i> You've reached the voicemail
of Charlotte Spencer.</i>


00:14:52.687 --> 00:14:54.527
<i> Please leave a message
at the tone.</i>


00:14:55.891 --> 00:14:57.860
Um, Charlotte, hi.
This is Helen.


00:14:57.891 --> 00:14:59.421
I'm sorry to keep missing you.


00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:02.801
I'm Sheila's friend
from the club.


00:15:04.765 --> 00:15:06.265
I really need some advice.


00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:07.610
Um...


00:15:07.634 --> 00:15:10.263
So if you have a moment, I'd
appreciate you returning my call.


00:15:10.302 --> 00:15:11.402
Thank you.


00:15:24.583 --> 00:15:25.860
<i>Can I get you anything?</i>


00:15:25.884 --> 00:15:27.684
<i>Uh, water, please.</i>


00:15:27.719 --> 00:15:29.119
Still or sparkling?


00:15:29.154 --> 00:15:31.724
Tap's good, uh, no ice, please.


00:15:32.824 --> 00:15:35.264
- Helen.
- Charlotte.


00:15:41.298 --> 00:15:44.428
Let me be the first to say,
with total conviction,


00:15:44.468 --> 00:15:46.798
that I actually do know
what you're going through.


00:15:49.406 --> 00:15:51.615
First off,
I invited you to meet me here,


00:15:51.641 --> 00:15:53.811
so I absolutely insist
on treating you.


00:15:53.843 --> 00:15:55.783
-Oh, that's not necessary...
- I said I insist.


00:15:57.046 --> 00:15:59.086
I'm sure you're used to
getting your way.


00:15:59.115 --> 00:16:01.185
Well, I have been told
I'm difficult to refuse.


00:16:01.217 --> 00:16:03.117
- Good afternoon, ladies.


00:16:03.153 --> 00:16:04.053
Afternoon.


00:16:04.087 --> 00:16:06.086
We will have
the Afternoon Tea Service


00:16:06.121 --> 00:16:07.961
and two glasses of champagne.


00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:09.990
Very good, madam.


00:16:10.025 --> 00:16:11.794
Just because
we're meeting for tea


00:16:11.826 --> 00:16:13.427
doesn't mean
we can't drink champagne.


00:16:16.498 --> 00:16:18.568
So, how are you holding up?


00:16:20.268 --> 00:16:22.068
Honestly, I'm not sure.


00:16:22.102 --> 00:16:24.412
-He's been gone... Andy, yes?
- Yes, Andy.


00:16:24.439 --> 00:16:26.069
He was taken how long ago?


00:16:26.106 --> 00:16:28.706
Uh, we lost contact with him,


00:16:28.743 --> 00:16:31.153
two and a half months Friday.


00:16:31.712 --> 00:16:33.251
Who else is in the loop?


00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.380
Sheila. Now, you.


00:16:34.414 --> 00:16:36.614
But Sheila tells me you've
been in touch with the FBI?


00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:37.950
Oh, yes. Yeah.


00:16:37.985 --> 00:16:39.814
And they've been
utterly useless.


00:16:40.487 --> 00:16:42.157
Well, they're very nice guys.


00:16:42.188 --> 00:16:43.888
Well, that's part
of the problem.


00:16:43.923 --> 00:16:45.633
-You think so?
- Well, yes. They talk nice.


00:16:45.659 --> 00:16:46.828
But they don't do anything


00:16:46.859 --> 00:16:49.399
unless they're
absolutely forced.


00:16:49.428 --> 00:16:50.798
Ladies.


00:16:56.134 --> 00:16:57.934
- Shall I pour the tea?
- No.


00:16:59.971 --> 00:17:01.880
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.


00:17:07.844 --> 00:17:09.615
To the safe return of your son.


00:17:09.647 --> 00:17:11.047
Thank you.


00:17:11.549 --> 00:17:12.589
To Andy.


00:17:19.856 --> 00:17:21.525
Can I ask you
a personal question?


00:17:22.793 --> 00:17:24.723
Sure.


00:17:24.761 --> 00:17:26.521
Why haven't you
reached out more?


00:17:26.564 --> 00:17:28.793
They told me
not to tell anybody.


00:17:28.831 --> 00:17:30.631
- Who, the FBI?
- Yeah.


00:17:30.666 --> 00:17:32.366
Oh, that's so stupid.


00:17:32.401 --> 00:17:34.830
Well, they said his life
would be in danger.


00:17:34.869 --> 00:17:36.900
Well, I'm sorry, Helen.


00:17:38.208 --> 00:17:40.348
If they think they can
manipulate you, they will.


00:17:41.376 --> 00:17:42.516
I realize that.


00:17:42.544 --> 00:17:43.544
I'm sorry.


00:17:43.578 --> 00:17:45.122
This brings it all back
to when Leo was taken.


00:17:45.146 --> 00:17:47.556
I guess I have
some unresolved anger.


00:17:50.385 --> 00:17:51.625
How is Leo?


00:17:53.721 --> 00:17:55.320
Good days and bad days.


00:17:55.355 --> 00:17:58.525
He's teaching Media Studies
at Stanford.


00:17:58.559 --> 00:18:00.889
By the way, I looked at
some of Andy's videos online.


00:18:00.927 --> 00:18:02.896
They're really very impressive.


00:18:02.929 --> 00:18:06.300
I... I haven't watched them.


00:18:06.333 --> 00:18:08.533
You should.
It's really very powerful.


00:18:08.569 --> 00:18:10.368
You know,
all the bombs going off


00:18:10.403 --> 00:18:12.703
and being shot at
and everything, I just...


00:18:12.738 --> 00:18:13.938
I can't.


00:18:14.874 --> 00:18:17.273
I feel the same way
about Leo's work.


00:18:17.309 --> 00:18:19.740
When he was a student,
he talked about journalism


00:18:19.779 --> 00:18:21.879
like it was a sacred calling.


00:18:21.914 --> 00:18:24.423
I was so proud of him.
I encouraged him.


00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:28.390
Then when he shipped himself
off to Kandahar,


00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:32.360
<i>I'd wished we had canceled our
subscription to the Times years ago.</i>


00:18:33.792 --> 00:18:37.161
I don't really know
where Andy gets it.


00:18:37.194 --> 00:18:39.004
Well, aren't you
an emergency room nurse?


00:18:39.463 --> 00:18:40.863
So?


00:18:40.898 --> 00:18:42.068
You don't see the parallels?


00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:44.669
No, I don't put my life
on the line.


00:18:48.839 --> 00:18:50.239
I have to ask you.


00:18:50.841 --> 00:18:53.041
How did you get him back?


00:18:53.076 --> 00:18:56.916
Hmm. Certainly not by
being quiet about it.


00:18:57.412 --> 00:18:59.222
Who'd you talk to?


00:19:00.984 --> 00:19:03.414
We have friends who have friends.


00:19:04.386 --> 00:19:06.216
Yeah, I don't have
those kind of friends.


00:19:06.255 --> 00:19:08.085
Well, you don't know
unless you ask.


00:19:08.123 --> 00:19:10.383
Nobody I know
has that kind of money.


00:19:10.426 --> 00:19:11.495
What kind of money?


00:19:13.628 --> 00:19:15.399
Ransom money.


00:19:15.431 --> 00:19:18.040
We didn't pay a ransom
to release Leo.


00:19:19.733 --> 00:19:21.063
Did the military go in?


00:19:21.102 --> 00:19:22.962
No, no, they don't do that.


00:19:25.338 --> 00:19:27.316
I feel like you're telling me
to read between the lines,


00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:31.051
but I don't even see
the lines, so I don't get it.


00:19:31.579 --> 00:19:33.318
Well,


00:19:33.346 --> 00:19:34.986
there's a balance to be struck


00:19:35.015 --> 00:19:37.015
between asserting yourself


00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.859
and coming on too strong.


00:19:38.885 --> 00:19:40.315
Okay.


00:19:41.487 --> 00:19:44.028
I have to admit,
I sometimes wonder


00:19:44.057 --> 00:19:45.756
if I would have done better


00:19:45.791 --> 00:19:48.121
had I been more
anonymous myself.


00:19:48.694 --> 00:19:50.394
What does that mean?


00:19:50.429 --> 00:19:53.538
Well, the more people who know,
the more false leads you get.


00:19:53.564 --> 00:19:55.004
The more e-mails,


00:19:55.033 --> 00:19:56.934
from Pakistan, Qatar,


00:19:56.969 --> 00:19:59.208
telling you that for
$10,000 in Bitcoin


00:19:59.237 --> 00:20:01.177
they can give you
the GPS coordinates


00:20:01.205 --> 00:20:04.045
of where the terrorist
is keeping your son.


00:20:04.075 --> 00:20:05.745
And maybe they can.
Maybe they do know.


00:20:07.611 --> 00:20:11.852
So you have to deal with the
consequences of your decision.


00:20:11.883 --> 00:20:16.252
Do you scrape together enough
money to spread around some


00:20:16.287 --> 00:20:19.627
dubious Middle Eastern
bribery network?


00:20:19.657 --> 00:20:20.666
Or,


00:20:21.925 --> 00:20:25.266
<i>do you just decide to swallow
the awful thought</i>


00:20:25.295 --> 00:20:27.734
<i> that maybe you could have
done something more?</i>


00:20:52.052 --> 00:20:54.123
Can I ask you something?


00:20:54.155 --> 00:20:56.694
Excuse me. Excuse me,
I have a question.


00:20:57.524 --> 00:21:01.233
I may be, uh, wiring
a large sum of money


00:21:01.261 --> 00:21:03.331
to another country, and I...


00:21:03.363 --> 00:21:05.273
How do you do that from here?


00:21:07.001 --> 00:21:09.740
Oh, no I already saw
this form online.


00:21:09.769 --> 00:21:11.409
And what it says is that, uh,


00:21:11.437 --> 00:21:15.206
if you want to transfer over
$10,000 internationally,


00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:16.617
you have to get some
kind of permission,


00:21:16.641 --> 00:21:17.811
so that's why I'm here.


00:21:18.811 --> 00:21:20.751
To ask you for permission.


00:21:23.315 --> 00:21:24.545
Where's the money going?


00:21:25.984 --> 00:21:28.614
Let's say, um, Syria.


00:21:28.653 --> 00:21:32.182
Could you send a large
amount of money to Syria?


00:21:32.824 --> 00:21:34.754
S-Y-R-I-A.


00:21:38.696 --> 00:21:39.826
Nope.


00:21:39.863 --> 00:21:41.323
Turkey?


00:21:41.365 --> 00:21:42.535
Call the number on the form.


00:21:42.566 --> 00:21:44.465
No, look, how much
could I send to Turkey?


00:21:44.501 --> 00:21:47.461
- Next in line, please.
- No, not next in line.


00:21:47.504 --> 00:21:49.634
I asked you a fucking question.


00:22:06.322 --> 00:22:08.052
- Can I... Can I...
- Oh.


00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:09.820
- The bedrooms?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.


00:22:23.404 --> 00:22:25.473
Water pressure's really strong.


00:22:30.310 --> 00:22:32.740
<i>Can we list it
for a little bit more?</i>


00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:35.610
<i>Well, it's what
the market will hold.</i>


00:22:35.649 --> 00:22:36.749
<i>I mean,</i>


00:22:37.351 --> 00:22:39.320
it may even be a teardown.


00:22:50.997 --> 00:22:52.856
Can we do it without
a sign on the lawn?


00:22:54.433 --> 00:22:56.133
Not if you want it to sell.


00:23:06.377 --> 00:23:09.277
Look, Miss Sterling, you told me
you wanted to sell this urgently.


00:23:19.488 --> 00:23:20.632
<i>Significant
turn of events today,</i>


00:23:20.656 --> 00:23:23.726
<i>as the last Islamic
stronghold of Syria,</i>


00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:27.370
<i>the city of Abu Kamal
has been liberated.</i>


00:23:27.397 --> 00:23:29.327
<i>You're seeing photos
here from the area</i>


00:23:29.365 --> 00:23:32.235
<i>where government forces
report that militias from</i>


00:23:32.268 --> 00:23:34.907
<i>both Syria and Iran
have joined forces.</i>


00:24:11.304 --> 00:24:13.374
Oh, thank you, sweetie.


00:24:34.792 --> 00:24:36.236
- Do you know where my daughter is?


00:24:36.260 --> 00:24:38.172
- What's your daughter's name?
- The name's Kayla.


00:24:38.196 --> 00:24:39.966
- Her name's Kayla?
- Yes.


00:24:39.998 --> 00:24:42.107
She went in the ambulance
before me.


00:24:42.132 --> 00:24:43.309
- Well, we're gonna find her.
- Okay.


00:24:43.333 --> 00:24:44.511
We're gonna find her.
Let's see here.


00:24:44.535 --> 00:24:45.878
I let her go in the
ambulance without me.


00:24:45.902 --> 00:24:47.446
Right. Well, that's
the right thing to do.


00:24:47.470 --> 00:24:48.547
We're going to find her.
Sit down.


00:24:48.571 --> 00:24:49.714
Anybody call anesthesia?


00:24:49.738 --> 00:24:51.416
Multiple gunshot wounds.
Coming in.


00:24:51.440 --> 00:24:54.202
<i>We have seven
victims, expecting multiple traumas.</i>


00:24:54.577 --> 00:24:56.146
<i>We need more ambulances.</i>


00:24:56.178 --> 00:24:57.778
Please. Please.


00:24:57.813 --> 00:24:59.013
Please!


00:24:59.048 --> 00:25:00.678
BP is a 100 over 70.


00:25:00.716 --> 00:25:02.585
Tell me the damn...
-Yes.


00:25:02.617 --> 00:25:04.217
We need to intubate immediately.


00:25:04.252 --> 00:25:07.423
Has anyone tried to
contact any of their parents?


00:25:07.456 --> 00:25:09.825
He just walked in
and just started shooting.


00:25:09.858 --> 00:25:11.828
He's not gonna make it, Reza.


00:25:11.860 --> 00:25:12.860
Helen.


00:25:20.669 --> 00:25:22.799
Reza, call it.


00:25:22.837 --> 00:25:24.266
I'm the doctor.


00:25:24.305 --> 00:25:27.035
Dr. Rahimi, there are other
patients that need you.


00:25:31.077 --> 00:25:33.848
Time of death, 2:33.


00:25:35.583 --> 00:25:39.322
Michelle, cross-check
and get it to the OR.


00:25:54.066 --> 00:25:55.396
It's time.


00:25:56.200 --> 00:25:57.570
Get cleaned up.


00:26:21.091 --> 00:26:23.321
Jerry, can I just take a minute?


00:27:07.366 --> 00:27:09.136
I'm sorry.


00:27:27.252 --> 00:27:28.992
What are you going to say
to the family?


00:27:31.323 --> 00:27:32.623
I don't know.


00:27:35.225 --> 00:27:36.855
You've got to be clear.


00:27:36.894 --> 00:27:38.064
You've got to be strong.


00:27:38.095 --> 00:27:40.596
This is the worst news
they're ever going to hear,


00:27:40.632 --> 00:27:43.501
and nothing you can say
is going to make it better.


00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:46.200
Be clear, be strong.


00:27:46.237 --> 00:27:47.607
Practice on me.


00:27:50.206 --> 00:27:51.636
Um...


00:27:52.374 --> 00:27:54.475
I... I regret
to inform you...


00:27:54.511 --> 00:27:56.950
No, stop. It's not about
you and your regret.


00:27:56.979 --> 00:27:58.919
Be clear. Be strong.


00:28:02.617 --> 00:28:04.717
Your son didn't make it.


00:28:04.753 --> 00:28:06.853
We did everything we could.


00:28:06.889 --> 00:28:09.089
I'm so very sorry for your loss.


00:28:11.960 --> 00:28:13.030
Good.


00:28:14.329 --> 00:28:15.598
Do it just like that.


00:28:41.687 --> 00:28:44.526
I'm looking for
the parents of...


00:28:48.493 --> 00:28:50.292
Your son didn't make it.


00:28:50.328 --> 00:28:52.039
He died. We did
everything we could...


00:28:52.064 --> 00:28:55.064
What are you saying?
What are you talking about?


00:28:55.100 --> 00:28:56.999
You didn't do anything!


00:28:57.034 --> 00:28:59.074
You didn't do anything!


00:30:34.158 --> 00:30:36.028
Eighty kinds of oil
at the Hannaford's now,


00:30:36.059 --> 00:30:38.629
this is the only one
that's any good.


00:30:38.662 --> 00:30:40.721
But I love the way
they've remodeled.


00:30:40.763 --> 00:30:42.293
It looks really great.
Right?


00:30:42.331 --> 00:30:43.932
It's a consumer's paradise.


00:30:43.968 --> 00:30:47.637
They throw away more food in a day
than I saw in a month in Kabul.


00:30:47.671 --> 00:30:49.771
Well, they do donate a lot
of it to the group home.


00:30:49.806 --> 00:30:51.946
They're very good with
the community that way.


00:30:51.974 --> 00:30:54.073
It's good PR
that costs them nothing.


00:30:54.109 --> 00:30:55.920
<i>...killed at least 40 people</i>


00:30:55.944 --> 00:30:58.075
<i>and wounded dozens more...</i>


00:31:02.718 --> 00:31:04.158
You don't want to hear it?


00:31:04.186 --> 00:31:05.356
Not secondhand.


00:31:10.591 --> 00:31:12.392
Okay, why are you so angry?


00:31:12.428 --> 00:31:13.998
I'm not angry, Mom.


00:31:18.199 --> 00:31:19.759
I'm frustrated.


00:31:21.935 --> 00:31:23.605
-I'm totally useless here.


00:31:23.637 --> 00:31:25.508
Baby, you're not useless.


00:31:25.539 --> 00:31:26.939
I don't want to hurt
your feelings,


00:31:26.974 --> 00:31:28.917
but there's no way you can
understand what I'm going through.


00:31:28.941 --> 00:31:30.853
Well, how can I understand it
when you don't talk to me


00:31:30.877 --> 00:31:34.247
and you keep it all
locked inside you?


00:31:43.222 --> 00:31:44.692
It's not enough for me here.


00:31:47.727 --> 00:31:49.087
It's never been.


00:31:50.528 --> 00:31:51.828
This life...


00:31:53.132 --> 00:31:54.402
This way of living.


00:31:55.567 --> 00:31:57.196
I'm suffocating.


00:31:59.536 --> 00:32:00.836
Well...


00:32:00.871 --> 00:32:02.970
Maybe it's time for you
to get your own place.


00:32:03.006 --> 00:32:04.506
Oh! Where?


00:32:04.541 --> 00:32:05.841
Downtown Oneonta?


00:32:07.078 --> 00:32:08.878
So I can be close to the action?


00:32:09.980 --> 00:32:11.350
Another meth-head arrested


00:32:11.381 --> 00:32:13.381
<i>and I get the front page
article in the Daily Star?</i>


00:32:15.385 --> 00:32:18.284
Oh, you always looked down on
everyone and everything here.


00:32:18.320 --> 00:32:20.290
Right? You're so much
better than everybody


00:32:20.322 --> 00:32:22.563
and I'm just stupid
and I can't understand


00:32:22.592 --> 00:32:23.691
'cause I'm just dumb!


00:32:23.726 --> 00:32:25.656
Damn it, you want this
to be about you!


00:32:26.629 --> 00:32:27.969
I'm not your partner, Mom.


00:32:29.331 --> 00:32:30.301
I love you,


00:32:30.333 --> 00:32:33.302
but I'm sick of feeling
responsible for you


00:32:33.335 --> 00:32:34.565
every time I make a decision.


00:32:34.602 --> 00:32:36.213
Oh, please.
Make a decision.


00:32:36.238 --> 00:32:39.037
I would love for you to make
a decision as a grown-up!


00:32:39.074 --> 00:32:42.744
Go ahead. And just don't
drag me into your drama.


00:32:44.678 --> 00:32:46.348
I have made a decision.


00:32:47.648 --> 00:32:48.918
I'm going back.


00:33:04.698 --> 00:33:07.237
You know what I'm confused about...
And maybe I'm wrong,


00:33:07.266 --> 00:33:10.236
but I thought that you would
be a lot more used to violence,


00:33:10.269 --> 00:33:11.279
coming from Iran.


00:33:12.170 --> 00:33:13.330
- Iran?
- Yeah.


00:33:14.206 --> 00:33:17.246
No. They arrest you
for having a gun.


00:33:17.276 --> 00:33:18.446
Really?


00:33:18.478 --> 00:33:19.677
Right. Yeah.


00:33:19.711 --> 00:33:22.381
Anyone in the mood
for some day-old cake?


00:33:22.981 --> 00:33:24.241
I'll pass.


00:33:26.717 --> 00:33:27.917
Helen, um...


00:33:27.951 --> 00:33:30.121
Is Andy coming home
for Christmas?


00:33:32.423 --> 00:33:33.752
January.


00:33:33.791 --> 00:33:36.661
You want me to cover
Christmas shift?


00:33:36.693 --> 00:33:38.663
Mmm, am I that obvious?


00:33:38.696 --> 00:33:40.565
You got it, boss,
but you owe me.


00:33:40.596 --> 00:33:41.836
Thank you.


00:33:41.864 --> 00:33:43.264
All right, I'm going in.


00:33:44.633 --> 00:33:46.473
Oh, hold on.
Wait for me.


00:34:02.284 --> 00:34:03.484
Good morning, Amy.


00:34:05.221 --> 00:34:07.590
How is your arm today?


00:34:07.621 --> 00:34:09.861
Jeez, I keep forgetting
I got shot.


00:34:10.458 --> 00:34:11.718
Arm's fine.


00:34:11.759 --> 00:34:13.929
Kayla is stable.


00:34:13.962 --> 00:34:16.332
Maybe you want to get some rest.


00:34:16.363 --> 00:34:18.373
Am I on some kind of
painkillers or something?


00:34:18.399 --> 00:34:20.968
It's weird, 'cause
I can't feel anything.


00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:22.240
I mean, like, anything.


00:34:24.137 --> 00:34:25.607
Amy, how's your shoulder?


00:34:25.639 --> 00:34:28.109
It's fine. I think you
should check on my daughter.


00:34:30.076 --> 00:34:31.846
I'm trying.
If I could just...


00:34:31.879 --> 00:34:33.089
Amy, why don't you come with me,


00:34:33.113 --> 00:34:34.682
we'll get a cup of coffee


00:34:34.714 --> 00:34:38.214
and let Dr. Rahimi
do his tests.


00:34:47.526 --> 00:34:48.925
Dr. Rahimi's a good doctor.


00:34:48.959 --> 00:34:51.499
I can't even understand
what he's saying.


00:34:51.529 --> 00:34:53.674
Well, I'm going to tell you
something that I probably shouldn't,


00:34:53.698 --> 00:34:55.437
and that is that
he has been spending


00:34:55.465 --> 00:34:57.796
more time with Kayla than
any of this other patients.


00:34:57.835 --> 00:35:00.505
I'm sorry. Uh, we need
you right away, Helen.


00:35:00.539 --> 00:35:01.939
Oh, I'm sorry.


00:35:01.973 --> 00:35:03.902
Um, I'll take a rain check
on the coffee,


00:35:03.940 --> 00:35:05.780
and I'll find you
and explain to you


00:35:05.809 --> 00:35:07.509
everything we're doing
with Kayla, okay?


00:35:09.378 --> 00:35:11.789
- Okay, Helen.
- Okay.


00:35:11.815 --> 00:35:13.915
Cafeteria's on the third floor.


00:35:13.951 --> 00:35:15.561
-What's up?
- Auditor's on the way.


00:35:15.585 --> 00:35:17.984
I need to get the snacks and
coffee out of the break room.


00:35:18.021 --> 00:35:20.281
- All of our snacks?
- Yes, it's a mess in there.


00:35:20.322 --> 00:35:22.951
Can you please sign off
the check sheets?


00:35:22.991 --> 00:35:25.622
Yeah. Oh, shit. I thought I had.
I'm sorry.


00:35:25.661 --> 00:35:27.161
It's okay. All right.
Thanks, Helen.


00:35:31.533 --> 00:35:33.163
Good morning, Kayla.


00:35:34.002 --> 00:35:36.332
It's December 5th.
Can you hear me?


00:35:45.545 --> 00:35:47.915
<i>I just sent it to you.
Did you get it?</i>


00:35:48.615 --> 00:35:49.955
That number can't be right.


00:35:49.983 --> 00:35:52.623
They can't expect me
to raise $20 million.


00:35:54.755 --> 00:35:56.095
Okay.


00:35:57.091 --> 00:35:58.160
Yeah.


00:35:59.692 --> 00:36:01.262
Yes, I understand.


00:36:27.618 --> 00:36:29.018
Mom, I can't do this.


00:37:16.731 --> 00:37:18.041
Would you like some coffee?


00:37:18.065 --> 00:37:19.495
I'm good. Thanks.


00:37:30.110 --> 00:37:32.320
Thank you for coming in,
Miss Sterling.


00:37:32.345 --> 00:37:35.344
I hope it's not
too much trouble.


00:37:35.380 --> 00:37:38.490
Oh, not at all. I've been trying
to see you for a while now.


00:37:38.517 --> 00:37:41.786
And actually, I have an
appointment right across the plaza.


00:37:41.820 --> 00:37:44.181
So you're going to be
seeing the FBI?


00:37:44.223 --> 00:37:46.053
Yeah. Right after this.


00:37:46.092 --> 00:37:47.691
You guys don't talk
to each other?


00:37:47.726 --> 00:37:49.166
Is there anything
we should know?


00:37:50.195 --> 00:37:52.065
Yeah, I got an e-mail.


00:37:52.097 --> 00:37:54.496
Now, I know it's illegal
to pay any ransom,


00:37:54.531 --> 00:37:56.201
but I was thinking,


00:37:56.233 --> 00:37:57.933
what about a prisoner exchange?


00:37:57.968 --> 00:38:00.609
I know that a soldier
that went AWOL


00:38:00.638 --> 00:38:02.707
and got captured, that's
what you guys did there,


00:38:02.740 --> 00:38:04.100
a prisoner exchange, right?


00:38:04.141 --> 00:38:06.471
Apples and oranges.
Military and civilians.


00:38:06.510 --> 00:38:09.409
It's entirely different when you're
sent over there with a uniform.


00:38:09.445 --> 00:38:12.055
Oh. How is it
different, exactly?


00:38:12.081 --> 00:38:14.152
Well, as I'm sure,
the FBI told you,


00:38:14.184 --> 00:38:16.623
they consider this to be
a criminal investigation.


00:38:16.653 --> 00:38:19.053
- Right.
- Businessmen, tourists,


00:38:19.088 --> 00:38:21.758
they're over there on
their own volition.


00:38:21.791 --> 00:38:24.960
Whereas with men and women
who are serving our country,


00:38:24.993 --> 00:38:27.664
different rules
and practices apply.


00:38:27.697 --> 00:38:29.736
But Andy was serving
our country.


00:38:29.765 --> 00:38:30.965
He just wasn't in a uniform.


00:38:30.999 --> 00:38:32.599
I mean, he wasn't
there on vacation.


00:38:32.634 --> 00:38:35.174
Andrew was in a place
he should not have been.


00:38:37.672 --> 00:38:40.913
A lot of people think the military
shouldn't be in that place.


00:38:40.943 --> 00:38:42.912
Let's not debate politics.


00:38:42.943 --> 00:38:44.313
It's not politics.


00:38:44.845 --> 00:38:46.155
It's my son,


00:38:46.948 --> 00:38:48.678
who is an American citizen.


00:38:48.716 --> 00:38:53.115
Isn't it your job to protect
American citizens abroad?


00:38:53.152 --> 00:38:55.293
That is a part of my job, yes.


00:38:55.890 --> 00:38:57.619
My heart goes out to you,


00:38:57.657 --> 00:38:59.027
as it does to your boy,


00:38:59.058 --> 00:39:02.058
and every other person
in a conflict zone,


00:39:02.095 --> 00:39:03.354
whether they volunteered,


00:39:03.395 --> 00:39:06.165
or whether they found
themselves in a situation


00:39:06.198 --> 00:39:08.298
they were not
adequately prepared for.


00:39:08.333 --> 00:39:10.773
He's been a journalist for 15 years.
He was prepared.


00:39:10.802 --> 00:39:12.472
-Then he knew the risks.
- Yes.


00:39:12.504 --> 00:39:14.934
And I'm sure he wouldn't
want to risk other lives


00:39:14.973 --> 00:39:16.183
on a military operation


00:39:16.208 --> 00:39:18.947
that wasn't even guaranteed
to bring him home.


00:39:18.977 --> 00:39:20.377
Those people have families, too.


00:39:20.411 --> 00:39:23.422
So you feel it was Andy's
fault that he got captured,


00:39:23.448 --> 00:39:25.687
and you won't risk sending
your people in to help him?


00:39:25.716 --> 00:39:27.586
I hope you don't think
I'm suggesting that.


00:39:27.619 --> 00:39:30.719
It sounds like it.
What are you doing?


00:39:30.755 --> 00:39:32.954
Okay, look, this is
a very complicated process,


00:39:32.989 --> 00:39:35.829
and it needs to be handled by
people that understand the region.


00:39:35.859 --> 00:39:37.730
Right. Well,
who is that, then?


00:39:41.064 --> 00:39:43.134
I don't want to
disparage the FBI,


00:39:43.166 --> 00:39:44.895
but I do know from experience


00:39:44.933 --> 00:39:46.303
what is effective
and what is not.


00:39:46.335 --> 00:39:49.205
Then what is effective?
What is the plan?


00:39:49.238 --> 00:39:50.438
What are you gonna do?


00:39:50.472 --> 00:39:53.642
Unfortunately, Miss Sterling,
that information


00:39:53.675 --> 00:39:55.245
is classified.


00:39:56.879 --> 00:39:58.788
I'm his mother.


00:39:58.813 --> 00:40:00.243
You can rest assured


00:40:00.281 --> 00:40:03.211
knowing that we're doing
all that we can.


00:40:03.251 --> 00:40:05.322
Now, maybe it would help us all


00:40:05.354 --> 00:40:07.523
if you were to tell us what
progress the FBI has made.


00:40:07.555 --> 00:40:09.855
You know what? You can
fucking ask them yourself.


00:40:17.397 --> 00:40:18.574
<i>So, State Department.</i>


00:40:18.598 --> 00:40:19.809
<i>What did you guys
talk about over there?</i>


00:40:19.833 --> 00:40:22.933
<i>Can't you guys
just talk to each other?</i>


00:40:22.970 --> 00:40:24.770
Maybe I should take things
into my own hands.


00:40:24.805 --> 00:40:26.144
Be careful with that.


00:40:26.172 --> 00:40:29.712
Oh, okay. I'll shut up and let
the grown-ups handle everything.


00:40:29.742 --> 00:40:30.642
That's not what I meant.


00:40:30.676 --> 00:40:35.416
You are a crucial part
of this investigation.


00:40:35.448 --> 00:40:38.678
Yeah. Lying to everyone I know has
been vital to this investigation.


00:40:38.717 --> 00:40:40.256
It's keeping Andy alive.


00:40:42.821 --> 00:40:44.221
So...


00:40:44.255 --> 00:40:47.925
You want me to negotiate
the price of my son's life


00:40:47.959 --> 00:40:50.459
down further and further
on your behalf,


00:40:50.495 --> 00:40:53.535
even though you have
no intention of paying it?


00:40:53.565 --> 00:40:56.574
For what? Just to see
how low they'll go?


00:40:56.600 --> 00:40:59.440
There's a science
to negotiating, Helen.


00:40:59.470 --> 00:41:00.669
We study it.


00:41:00.703 --> 00:41:02.744
The longer we stay
in communication with them,


00:41:02.773 --> 00:41:04.713
the more we understand
who we're dealing with


00:41:04.741 --> 00:41:05.811
and what they really want.


00:41:05.843 --> 00:41:08.682
It's been three months.
What have you learned?


00:41:08.712 --> 00:41:09.752
You have to trust us.


00:41:09.779 --> 00:41:11.819
What do you think I've
been doing all this time,


00:41:11.848 --> 00:41:14.577
while you guys just play cat
and mouse with those fuckers?


00:41:14.617 --> 00:41:17.118
I swear to Christ, if
something happens to my child,


00:41:17.153 --> 00:41:19.663
because you're waiting
to sign off on some form...


00:41:26.461 --> 00:41:28.470
This is the response
we recommend.


00:41:29.531 --> 00:41:31.401
Where it says Proof of Life,


00:41:31.433 --> 00:41:35.242
you have to be very personal,
very specific.


00:41:35.269 --> 00:41:39.179
It has to be a question
only you would know to ask,


00:41:39.207 --> 00:41:40.777
and an answer
only he could answer.


00:43:10.124 --> 00:43:11.424
I don't wanna fight.


00:43:15.129 --> 00:43:16.499
You can smile.


00:44:05.476 --> 00:44:07.375
<i>Come on, Louganis, what you got?</i>


00:44:07.410 --> 00:44:08.620
<i>What you got?</i>


00:44:08.644 --> 00:44:10.814
<i>Oh! Oh, God!</i>


00:44:11.614 --> 00:44:13.184
<i>Oh, you ready?
You ready?</i>


00:44:13.216 --> 00:44:15.585
<i>Oh, my lord!</i>


00:44:15.618 --> 00:44:17.459
<i>How do you excuse that?</i>


00:44:17.487 --> 00:44:19.487
<i>Because I am not burning this.</i>


00:44:19.522 --> 00:44:21.451
<i>Of course it's in focus.</i>


00:44:22.658 --> 00:44:24.458
<i> Now if you were operating,
I don't know</i>


00:44:24.492 --> 00:44:26.522
<i>it'd be much more
questionable to me.</i>


00:44:26.561 --> 00:44:27.960
<i> Okay, all right, come here.</i>


00:44:29.731 --> 00:44:32.192
<i>This is my best friend, Sam.</i>


00:44:32.234 --> 00:44:33.564
<i>Say hello to the civilians.</i>


00:44:33.602 --> 00:44:36.501
<i>Hello. Hello, civilians.</i>


00:44:36.537 --> 00:44:37.877
<i> I love this man.</i>


00:44:37.905 --> 00:44:40.075
<i>He's taught me
everything worth knowing.</i>


00:44:40.108 --> 00:44:41.547
<i> Oh, then you're
in trouble, man.</i>


00:44:48.615 --> 00:44:50.385
<i> We are here, having fun!</i>


00:44:59.993 --> 00:45:02.362
<i>Classes have been
officially suspended here</i>


00:45:02.394 --> 00:45:03.994
<i>in the city of Homs,</i>


00:45:04.030 --> 00:45:07.360
<i>but every day, kids still gather
in the schoolyard for games.</i>


00:45:36.860 --> 00:45:38.430
<i>Allahu Akbar!</i>


00:45:54.242 --> 00:45:55.652
<i>As you can see,</i>


00:45:55.677 --> 00:45:58.207
<i> these attacks make no
distinction between civilian</i>


00:45:58.246 --> 00:45:59.816
<i>and military targets.</i>


00:45:59.848 --> 00:46:03.188
<i> Forty percent of the
casualties here are, like Yana,</i>


00:46:03.218 --> 00:46:05.857
<i>children under the age of 12.</i>


00:46:07.154 --> 00:46:08.754
<i> And the children who survive</i>


00:46:08.789 --> 00:46:12.329
<i> have lost their friends,
their school,</i>


00:46:12.360 --> 00:46:13.760
<i>and their faith</i>


00:46:13.794 --> 00:46:15.994
<i>that the most powerful
country in the world</i>


00:46:16.029 --> 00:46:17.469
<i>will come to protect them.</i>


00:46:24.438 --> 00:46:26.807
<i>Yeah. Charlotte?
Charlotte, this is Helen.</i>


00:46:27.340 --> 00:46:29.010
I...


00:46:31.111 --> 00:46:34.180
I'm overwhelmed. I would
appreciate you returning my call.


00:46:45.090 --> 00:46:49.499
All right, Kayla, I'm going to be
filling in for your mom tonight.


00:46:49.527 --> 00:46:52.337
<i>With The Sea of Knowledge.</i>


00:46:52.363 --> 00:46:54.963
"Now, it may be hard
to imagine it,


00:46:54.999 --> 00:46:57.209
"but this land was
once so barren,


00:46:57.235 --> 00:46:59.534
"it was called
the Kingdom of Salt.


00:46:59.570 --> 00:47:02.870
"The lush green hills that we
walk today were once so dry


00:47:02.906 --> 00:47:05.046
"and cracked that trees
could not grow here.


00:47:05.075 --> 00:47:08.015
<i>"No visitors had dared
enter the Kingdom,</i>


00:47:08.044 --> 00:47:11.144
<i>"for it was said terrible
monsters roamed the land.</i>


00:47:11.180 --> 00:47:13.809
<i>"But it was also said
that on the other side..."</i>


00:47:20.322 --> 00:47:22.192
Helen.


00:47:22.224 --> 00:47:23.994
Let's talk in my office.


00:47:35.169 --> 00:47:36.539
Helen, sit.


00:47:43.310 --> 00:47:45.110
This isn't Helen's fault.


00:47:45.145 --> 00:47:47.015
I forgot to sign the order.


00:47:47.047 --> 00:47:48.076
It's both of you.


00:47:48.114 --> 00:47:50.785
It's her access code and
your name is on the paper,


00:47:50.817 --> 00:47:52.747
and there's no patient name,
and now,


00:47:52.786 --> 00:47:55.245
the antibiotic count is short
in the middle of an audit.


00:47:55.288 --> 00:47:57.158
It's not
Dr. Rahimi's fault.


00:47:57.189 --> 00:47:59.301
It was Andy's ex-girlfriend,
and she didn't have insurance.


00:47:59.325 --> 00:48:02.084
We're two quarters away from
shutting down an entire wing, Helen.


00:48:02.127 --> 00:48:04.539
Well, I didn't become a nurse
to make a profit for a hospital.


00:48:04.563 --> 00:48:07.003
Don't do that.
Do not make this personal,


00:48:07.032 --> 00:48:09.001
it's not like you.


00:48:09.034 --> 00:48:11.364
We're not in
the miracles business.


00:48:11.403 --> 00:48:13.313
It's only luck and procedure.


00:48:13.338 --> 00:48:16.478
And the minute you start falling
in love with the patients,


00:48:16.508 --> 00:48:18.038
and reading to the patients,


00:48:18.076 --> 00:48:21.046
making exceptions to the
procedures, you lose trust.


00:48:25.449 --> 00:48:28.858
Are you okay, Helen? Is there
something going on with you?


00:48:34.257 --> 00:48:35.586
I'm fine.


00:48:41.230 --> 00:48:42.639
Keesha Thompson.


00:48:44.834 --> 00:48:47.034
And some soup,
Mary. Thanks.


00:48:48.637 --> 00:48:50.106
Here you go, Helen.


00:48:50.138 --> 00:48:51.338
Thank you.


00:48:58.345 --> 00:49:01.086
<i>I'm here because I was
told you were overwhelmed.</i>


00:49:01.115 --> 00:49:03.614
Look, I worked in
the same region as Andy


00:49:03.651 --> 00:49:05.581
just before he was taken.


00:49:06.521 --> 00:49:07.681
I would have called first,


00:49:07.721 --> 00:49:10.050
but Sheila said privacy
is important to you.


00:49:10.089 --> 00:49:12.920
Yeah, so you
show up at my place of work?


00:49:14.462 --> 00:49:16.761
It's not right that
they're forcing you


00:49:16.796 --> 00:49:18.636
to keep this all to yourself.


00:49:21.768 --> 00:49:24.177
Look, I don't want to
endanger him any further.


00:49:24.203 --> 00:49:26.173
Well, secrecy isn't
going to help him.


00:49:26.204 --> 00:49:29.345
We need the media and
public outrage to help us.


00:49:29.376 --> 00:49:30.675
You need to go public with this.


00:49:30.709 --> 00:49:31.909
The FBI explained to me...


00:49:31.944 --> 00:49:35.684
I'm sure they told you
a lot of things,


00:49:35.714 --> 00:49:37.414
but we don't think
Andy would want you


00:49:37.449 --> 00:49:40.279
to trust the FBI to handle this.


00:49:40.318 --> 00:49:42.619
When Leo was taken, they
sent in the FBI at first...


00:49:42.654 --> 00:49:45.423
What... They sent in
the FBI for Leo?


00:49:45.456 --> 00:49:47.026
Yes.


00:49:47.058 --> 00:49:50.328
And it would have been comical if
it wasn't so utterly fucked up.


00:49:50.361 --> 00:49:53.900
People get seen talking with
huge Americans with buzz cuts,


00:49:53.930 --> 00:49:55.931
and two weeks later,
there's a local translator


00:49:55.967 --> 00:49:58.196
getting beheaded on a video.


00:49:58.235 --> 00:49:59.645
- On a video?
- Yes.


00:49:59.669 --> 00:50:02.099
They make movies of this shit.


00:50:02.139 --> 00:50:05.308
As a warning to anyone who's
thinking about aiding the infidels.


00:50:07.609 --> 00:50:10.580
So you've spoken
with Charlotte Spencer?


00:50:10.614 --> 00:50:12.653
Yeah, I helped get
the money across the border


00:50:12.681 --> 00:50:13.721
for Leo's release.


00:50:13.749 --> 00:50:14.779
She didn't pay ransom.


00:50:14.817 --> 00:50:15.917
They all pay ransom.


00:50:15.951 --> 00:50:18.091
Would you fucking
keep your voice down?


00:50:22.891 --> 00:50:24.561
I wanted to get
those cochlear implants,


00:50:24.593 --> 00:50:25.902
but I can't afford them.


00:50:27.662 --> 00:50:29.002
I know. I guess
I could've picked


00:50:29.030 --> 00:50:30.507
something less loud
to take pictures of.


00:50:30.531 --> 00:50:33.470
Yeah, you could have picked a job
that wouldn't ruin your hearing


00:50:33.500 --> 00:50:34.900
and put your life in danger.


00:50:35.936 --> 00:50:37.237
Well...


00:50:37.271 --> 00:50:40.280
For better or worse,
I have my people already.


00:50:41.508 --> 00:50:43.108
And Andy is one of them.


00:50:46.313 --> 00:50:48.412
We don't have a union.


00:50:48.448 --> 00:50:49.818
We don't have
a news organization


00:50:49.849 --> 00:50:51.290
providing a security detail.


00:50:51.318 --> 00:50:53.717
We don't have major
networks insuring us.


00:50:53.753 --> 00:50:55.613
We have to be our own network.


00:50:55.655 --> 00:50:56.985
We have each other.


00:50:58.257 --> 00:51:01.396
I'm here for Andy the same
way Andy would find my dad


00:51:01.426 --> 00:51:02.966
if something happened to me.


00:51:02.994 --> 00:51:05.325
Now I know you've been told
to keep this all quiet,


00:51:05.364 --> 00:51:06.875
and that you're not allowed
to pay a dime.


00:51:06.899 --> 00:51:09.138
But there's only one thing
these assholes respond to,


00:51:09.168 --> 00:51:10.708
and it's money.


00:51:11.437 --> 00:51:12.807
So if you want,


00:51:12.838 --> 00:51:15.207
we can connect you with
people who won't rip you off.


00:51:15.973 --> 00:51:17.743
I'll fly over there myself.


00:51:35.458 --> 00:51:37.328
- Hello.
- Hi.


00:51:37.360 --> 00:51:38.760
- Thank you.
- Come on in.


00:51:38.795 --> 00:51:40.195
Thanks so much.


00:51:49.538 --> 00:51:50.998
Hey, you made it!


00:51:51.974 --> 00:51:53.714
- Helen, you want a beer?
- No, thanks.


00:51:53.742 --> 00:51:55.341
I'll take it, Sam.


00:52:02.516 --> 00:52:04.656
Great house. Beautiful.


00:52:04.686 --> 00:52:06.026
Ah, thank you.


00:52:06.053 --> 00:52:07.953
It was my grandfather's,
originally.


00:52:07.988 --> 00:52:08.988
Oh.


00:52:15.730 --> 00:52:18.959
Maybe I could
use the ladies' room?


00:52:18.998 --> 00:52:20.328
Sure.
It's up the stairs.


00:52:20.366 --> 00:52:22.766
You make a left at
the painting of the dancers.


00:52:22.802 --> 00:52:24.741
Oh, thanks.


00:53:16.886 --> 00:53:18.296
We knew it wouldn't be easy.


00:53:18.320 --> 00:53:20.890
She's gonna need
a lot more prep.


00:53:20.922 --> 00:53:24.052
This is not
her world, Charlotte.


00:53:24.092 --> 00:53:25.369
She is who she is, Sam.


00:53:25.393 --> 00:53:26.971
I'm not going to give her
elocution lessons.


00:53:26.995 --> 00:53:29.235
Well, we better
do something fast,


00:53:29.264 --> 00:53:31.933
before they move him again
and we have no one to talk to.


00:53:31.966 --> 00:53:34.166
Sure. Will you
help me carry these, please?


00:53:36.403 --> 00:53:39.433
Making jokes like that,
I'm gonna hire you.


00:53:39.473 --> 00:53:41.384
Would you like
your tea and crumpets at the usual hour?


00:53:41.408 --> 00:53:42.278
Of course.


00:53:42.310 --> 00:53:44.140
How is this
going to work, exactly?


00:53:44.178 --> 00:53:46.917
Who's responsible for what?


00:53:46.946 --> 00:53:49.216
With Leo, there was
a fundraising team


00:53:49.248 --> 00:53:51.488
and the team that
delivered the money abroad.


00:53:51.517 --> 00:53:54.257
Charlotte should obviously
take the lead on fundraising.


00:53:54.287 --> 00:53:56.327
You really think
you're going to be able


00:53:56.356 --> 00:53:57.496
to raise $20 million?


00:53:57.524 --> 00:53:59.993
Well, Loic's people will
help us negotiate it down.


00:54:00.025 --> 00:54:02.225
I have been working
with the FBI already


00:54:02.260 --> 00:54:03.572
-to help negotiate it down.
- No. No.


00:54:03.596 --> 00:54:05.496
I told you, those fuckers
are just trying to...


00:54:05.531 --> 00:54:08.831
- I don't want to hear it.
- Can we keep this civil please, Sam?


00:54:08.867 --> 00:54:10.937
Leo's not-for-profit account
is still open.


00:54:10.969 --> 00:54:12.269
We can wire the money
from there.


00:54:12.304 --> 00:54:13.943
No, we can't.


00:54:13.972 --> 00:54:16.342
<i>My contact at The Wall
Street Journal just told me</i>


00:54:16.373 --> 00:54:18.773
the Feds set up a whole new
set of SWIFT protocols


00:54:18.809 --> 00:54:21.509
to try to crack down on money
laundering to terrorists.


00:54:21.545 --> 00:54:24.385
Not-for-profits are
specifically being monitored.


00:54:24.415 --> 00:54:27.054
Apparently, there is a way
around it.


00:54:27.083 --> 00:54:29.123
It's sketchy,
but it is invisible.


00:54:29.152 --> 00:54:30.652
By sketchy, you mean illegal?


00:54:30.686 --> 00:54:33.256
- Helen, you know...
- The less you know the better.


00:54:34.523 --> 00:54:37.934
Helen, I promised you
we will keep you protected.


00:54:38.996 --> 00:54:40.795
<i>They're not geniuses,</i>


00:54:40.829 --> 00:54:43.499
and they're not saints. They're
just people. Like you and me.


00:54:43.532 --> 00:54:44.972
Like you, you mean.


00:54:48.035 --> 00:54:50.006
What am I supposed
to say to them?


00:54:50.773 --> 00:54:52.073
Well, there isn't a script.


00:54:52.107 --> 00:54:53.477
You'll need to improvize.


00:54:53.509 --> 00:54:56.308
Maybe I should have
taken elocution lessons.


00:55:01.915 --> 00:55:04.486
So what did you say to them
when Leo was taken?


00:55:06.220 --> 00:55:09.389
I told them they were part
of an elite group of people


00:55:09.423 --> 00:55:10.353
I had chosen.


00:55:10.390 --> 00:55:13.860
<i>That their actions now
would be anonymous,</i>


00:55:13.894 --> 00:55:16.463
<i>but that history would
make them heroes.</i>


00:55:20.400 --> 00:55:22.609
Charlotte tells me
you're from upstate.


00:55:23.569 --> 00:55:24.969
Oneonta.


00:55:25.003 --> 00:55:27.303
My son went to Cornell.


00:55:27.340 --> 00:55:28.680
Great school.


00:55:28.708 --> 00:55:30.007
It's no Harvard,


00:55:30.041 --> 00:55:32.312
but he's done well
enough for himself.


00:55:33.178 --> 00:55:34.778
Did you keep Andy local,


00:55:34.813 --> 00:55:36.882
send him to Cornell as well?


00:55:36.915 --> 00:55:39.655
No, Wayne State
on a scholarship.


00:55:39.684 --> 00:55:41.054
Ah.


00:55:41.085 --> 00:55:42.715
David's son
is also a journalist.


00:55:42.753 --> 00:55:43.983
Oh.


00:55:44.021 --> 00:55:47.222
<i>He's the Metro Editor
for the Washington Post.</i>


00:55:47.259 --> 00:55:48.999
Oh. Nice.


00:55:50.093 --> 00:55:53.263
So, is Leo enjoying Stanford?


00:55:53.297 --> 00:55:55.297
He loves teaching.
Chris was just out


00:55:55.332 --> 00:55:57.901
to see him deliver a lecture
for the Knight Fellowship.


00:55:57.934 --> 00:55:59.274
Give them both our regards.


00:56:01.839 --> 00:56:05.348
So, you ready to put
the squeeze on?


00:56:12.014 --> 00:56:14.755
My son Andy is a journalist.


00:56:15.752 --> 00:56:17.381
Well, you know that.


00:56:18.320 --> 00:56:19.320
And, uh...


00:56:20.923 --> 00:56:24.522
Right now, he's, uh,
in a serious situation.


00:56:24.558 --> 00:56:26.828
I would be in San Francisco
myself right now


00:56:26.860 --> 00:56:28.091
if it wasn't very serious.


00:56:28.130 --> 00:56:29.430
Right, it's very serious.


00:56:29.464 --> 00:56:31.163
I sent you the link
to Andy's work.


00:56:31.198 --> 00:56:32.698
You've seen his videos, yes?


00:56:32.733 --> 00:56:34.173
Incredible stuff.


00:56:35.236 --> 00:56:37.106
There are only
a handful of people


00:56:37.137 --> 00:56:39.666
doing the kind of work
that Andy is doing


00:56:39.706 --> 00:56:41.236
in the world.


00:56:41.274 --> 00:56:44.015
But he is unaffiliated,


00:56:44.045 --> 00:56:45.184
right, Helen?


00:56:45.211 --> 00:56:47.381
He doesn't work for
a major news organization.


00:56:47.413 --> 00:56:49.053
Well, they don't go in there.


00:56:49.082 --> 00:56:51.382
Maybe that's for a good reason.


00:56:52.585 --> 00:56:54.328
Well, when we
approached you for help with Leo,


00:56:54.352 --> 00:56:56.723
your commitment
to journalism was total.


00:56:57.924 --> 00:57:00.733
You and Chris are
our friends, Charlotte.


00:57:00.759 --> 00:57:02.599
And Helen is our friend.


00:57:02.628 --> 00:57:04.958
Chris and I have committed
to a 100,000 each


00:57:04.996 --> 00:57:06.525
to secure Andy's release.


00:57:10.669 --> 00:57:12.908
In order to have the right
to have an opinion,


00:57:12.937 --> 00:57:15.437
I need people like Andy and Leo


00:57:15.473 --> 00:57:19.013
over there, to inform me
what is actually happening


00:57:19.043 --> 00:57:21.552
in the most dangerous
places in the world.


00:57:26.050 --> 00:57:27.649
Who else is involved?


00:57:29.119 --> 00:57:30.859
Well, Helen has been
very discreet.


00:57:30.887 --> 00:57:32.087
You are the first.


00:57:35.991 --> 00:57:38.432
I can commit to 25.


00:57:45.033 --> 00:57:46.233
Twenty-five.


00:57:49.004 --> 00:57:51.804
Fifty. All right,
let's call that a start.


00:57:51.840 --> 00:57:53.451
Thank you.


00:57:53.476 --> 00:57:56.045
The Feds have set up a whole
new set of SWIFT protocols,


00:57:56.077 --> 00:57:58.917
so we will not be using
the nonprofit this time.


00:57:58.947 --> 00:58:00.157
On Monday, you'll get an invoice


00:58:00.181 --> 00:58:02.110
from Dudek, Roley, and Esser.


00:58:02.149 --> 00:58:04.989
A retainer. Good idea.


00:58:05.018 --> 00:58:08.628
So are you and Chris going to be
spending time in Aspen this season?


00:58:08.655 --> 00:58:10.655
Well, that
was originally the plan.


00:58:10.690 --> 00:58:13.260
But as it turns out, Leo has
a whole set of lectures...


00:58:13.293 --> 00:58:15.022
A-ha!
- ...during that time.


00:58:15.061 --> 00:58:17.261
So I would very much like
to be there for that.


00:58:17.296 --> 00:58:19.236
Yes, he's such a busy man.


00:58:19.265 --> 00:58:21.066
Excuse me, gentlemen.


00:58:21.101 --> 00:58:23.800
I have to catch my bus.


00:58:24.704 --> 00:58:25.704
Thank you.


00:58:29.674 --> 00:58:30.844
Excuse me.


00:58:42.386 --> 00:58:45.056
Well, it wasn't as much
as we expected,


00:58:45.089 --> 00:58:46.589
but it's a good start.


00:58:49.526 --> 00:58:52.336
I hate myself for being
so angry with Andy


00:58:52.363 --> 00:58:54.103
for putting us all through this,


00:58:54.131 --> 00:58:56.100
but I just can't help it.
I'm sorry,


00:58:56.132 --> 00:58:58.172
but I'm furious.


00:58:58.201 --> 00:59:00.571
Begging strangers for money.


00:59:01.037 --> 00:59:02.637
It's just...


00:59:04.173 --> 00:59:05.743
It's not who I am.


00:59:09.578 --> 00:59:14.248
It was about six months
after Leo got home.


00:59:14.283 --> 00:59:16.423
In the middle of the night,
Chris's phone rang.


00:59:16.452 --> 00:59:18.129
I used to be able
to sleep through anything


00:59:18.153 --> 00:59:19.893
but ever since Leo was taken...


00:59:22.124 --> 00:59:24.933
So I was up,
so I went into Leo's room,


00:59:24.959 --> 00:59:27.059
sat on the end of his bed


00:59:27.095 --> 00:59:28.955
like I used to do
when he was a little boy,


00:59:28.997 --> 00:59:30.167
and I reached over,


00:59:30.196 --> 00:59:31.627
and he was gone.


00:59:32.733 --> 00:59:34.273
I panicked.


00:59:34.302 --> 00:59:37.411
I ran through the house
turning on all the lights.


00:59:37.437 --> 00:59:39.237
I ran back into his room,


00:59:39.272 --> 00:59:41.812
turned on the light, and I
saw that his window was open.


00:59:43.543 --> 00:59:45.573
So I ran outside
to the backyard,


00:59:45.612 --> 00:59:46.822
and there he was.


00:59:46.846 --> 00:59:49.886
He was sound asleep
on the frozen ground.


00:59:51.817 --> 00:59:54.257
I looked at him for a minute.


00:59:54.286 --> 00:59:56.356
I went back inside.
I made some coffee.


00:59:56.388 --> 00:59:58.187
Cooked some eggs.


00:59:59.258 --> 01:00:00.628
You just carry on.


01:00:01.760 --> 01:00:03.230
Making believe.


01:00:03.261 --> 01:00:05.670
Make believe that
everything's all right.


01:00:07.465 --> 01:00:08.895
It's what mothers do.


01:00:16.674 --> 01:00:19.173
<i>"He pushed his boat
into the water</i>


01:00:19.209 --> 01:00:21.079
and pulled himself
onto the deck.


01:00:21.111 --> 01:00:23.181
For the first time, Prince Henry


01:00:23.213 --> 01:00:25.482
was headed into
the open sea."


01:00:37.326 --> 01:00:39.026
"Prince Henry took a ladle
from his bucket


01:00:39.062 --> 01:00:43.162
and filled the Salt King's
stone chalice."


01:00:43.199 --> 01:00:46.028
- Hi.
- Amy.


01:00:46.067 --> 01:00:47.907
How was she last night?


01:00:47.936 --> 01:00:49.606
Well, there hasn't been


01:00:49.637 --> 01:00:51.107
any change for a long time.


01:00:51.139 --> 01:00:52.569
That's good, right?


01:00:56.978 --> 01:00:58.438
You want me to be
honest with you?


01:00:59.280 --> 01:01:00.949
Yeah, I wish somebody would be.


01:01:01.916 --> 01:01:03.326
You can, um...


01:01:03.351 --> 01:01:06.651
You can keep her ventilated
for as long as you want.


01:01:11.659 --> 01:01:13.758
You don't think that
she's going to make it?


01:01:15.862 --> 01:01:16.862
Okay.


01:01:18.798 --> 01:01:19.928
When, um...


01:01:21.066 --> 01:01:22.967
You and Joey and Kayla came in,


01:01:23.002 --> 01:01:25.172
we knew right away that Joey
wasn't going to make it.


01:01:25.204 --> 01:01:27.813
And I tried
to convince his parents


01:01:27.839 --> 01:01:29.779
to donate his organs,


01:01:29.808 --> 01:01:31.338
which seems


01:01:32.077 --> 01:01:33.647
really cold, but,


01:01:35.245 --> 01:01:37.416
I've had to watch
a lot of kids die,


01:01:37.449 --> 01:01:38.779
some of them...


01:01:39.885 --> 01:01:41.584
Some of them can't be helped.


01:01:41.618 --> 01:01:44.018
But there are other times
they die because


01:01:44.054 --> 01:01:47.384
they need a lung or a kidney...


01:01:47.424 --> 01:01:50.393
So you want me
to donate her organs?


01:01:50.427 --> 01:01:52.158
- You want me to unplug her?
- No.


01:01:52.196 --> 01:01:54.626
You don't...
I'm not saying that.


01:01:54.665 --> 01:01:57.464
You don't... You can keep
her on the ventilator


01:01:57.500 --> 01:01:59.610
for as long as you want.


01:02:00.803 --> 01:02:02.802
All I'm saying is,


01:02:02.838 --> 01:02:05.339
what happened to you
and Joey and Kayla


01:02:06.042 --> 01:02:07.552
was meaningless.


01:02:08.544 --> 01:02:10.273
It didn't happen for a reason,


01:02:10.312 --> 01:02:11.590
it didn't happen because
it was God's plan,


01:02:11.614 --> 01:02:13.214
or because it happened
for the best.


01:02:13.248 --> 01:02:15.448
It was just stupid,


01:02:16.051 --> 01:02:17.551
and senseless.


01:02:19.922 --> 01:02:20.982
But...


01:02:23.792 --> 01:02:26.092
When you're dealt a shitty hand,


01:02:28.196 --> 01:02:29.665
what you do with it


01:02:31.165 --> 01:02:32.635
doesn't have to be.


01:02:55.655 --> 01:02:58.094
<i>I pray for her every day.</i>


01:02:58.123 --> 01:03:00.423
<i>I'm sure her mother
appreciates that.</i>


01:03:02.862 --> 01:03:04.391
You don't pray?


01:03:06.297 --> 01:03:08.507
No. Not for
a very long time.


01:03:36.392 --> 01:03:38.391
<i>That's it! Three.</i>


01:03:39.561 --> 01:03:41.331
<i>Four. Give me
your energy!</i>


01:03:41.362 --> 01:03:44.173
<i>Five. Six.</i>


01:03:44.200 --> 01:03:45.729
<i>Two more. Seven.</i>


01:03:46.935 --> 01:03:49.065
<i>Eight. Here, two.</i>


01:03:49.104 --> 01:03:50.574
<i>Your tricep!</i>


01:03:50.605 --> 01:03:54.504
<i>And one, two, three, four.</i>


01:03:54.542 --> 01:03:55.812
<i>Here comes...</i>


01:03:59.180 --> 01:04:00.780
<i>Hello, ladies and gentlemen.</i>


01:04:00.815 --> 01:04:04.045
<i>And welcome to episode one
of the wilderness series.</i>


01:04:05.419 --> 01:04:09.018
<i>The Nurse
in her natural habitat.</i>


01:04:09.055 --> 01:04:10.955
<i>Always approach carefully,</i>


01:04:10.990 --> 01:04:14.730
<i>especially if the Wild Nurse
has not had her coffee yet.</i>


01:04:17.363 --> 01:04:19.792
<i>The Wild Nurse stirs.</i>


01:04:19.832 --> 01:04:23.262
<i> Andy? What are you doing
with that thing?</i>


01:04:23.301 --> 01:04:25.642
<i>The Wild Nurse is awakening.</i>


01:04:27.272 --> 01:04:28.702
<i>Give me that camera.</i>


01:04:30.675 --> 01:04:32.705
<i>I'm not even dressed yet.</i>


01:04:33.878 --> 01:04:34.978
<i>Sorry.</i>


01:04:36.547 --> 01:04:38.947
<i>There, how does that feel?</i>


01:04:40.685 --> 01:04:41.715
<i>We'll be right back.</i>


01:04:41.752 --> 01:04:43.582
<i>Oh, no.</i>


01:04:47.192 --> 01:04:49.121
<i>How do you turn this thing off?</i>


01:04:49.159 --> 01:04:50.869
<i> Right here.</i>


01:04:52.695 --> 01:04:54.535
<i> Peck ups! Two,</i>


01:04:54.565 --> 01:04:57.235
<i>roll to the front!
Warm up your legs.</i>


01:04:57.834 --> 01:04:58.934
<i>Uh!</i>


01:04:59.903 --> 01:05:02.232
<i>Uh! Uh!</i>


01:05:02.271 --> 01:05:04.901
<i>Start breathing, uh, inhale.</i>


01:05:05.875 --> 01:05:07.015
<i>Down.</i>


01:05:07.276 --> 01:05:08.476
<i>Tilt.</i>


01:05:23.091 --> 01:05:24.791
<i>- Helen?
- Yes, Loic.</i>


01:05:24.826 --> 01:05:26.996
<i>- Helen?
- How was he, Loic?</i>


01:05:27.028 --> 01:05:28.987
<i>Hello? Helen?</i>


01:05:29.029 --> 01:05:31.059
Yes. Can you see me?


01:05:32.833 --> 01:05:33.933
Fuck.


01:05:42.042 --> 01:05:44.441
<i>I'm sorry. The connection
is terrible.</i>


01:05:44.477 --> 01:05:47.807
I understand, but I didn't hear.
How is he?


01:05:48.514 --> 01:05:50.454
<i>He was the strongest man.</i>


01:05:50.483 --> 01:05:52.183
<i>- Was? "Was"?
- Is.</i>


01:05:52.218 --> 01:05:53.448
<i>Is.</i>


01:05:53.486 --> 01:05:56.515
<i> Is the strongest I ever meet.</i>


01:05:58.356 --> 01:05:59.600
<i>Forgive me, my English...</i>


01:05:59.624 --> 01:06:02.494
<i>- It's okay.
- Andy tries to teach, but...</i>


01:06:02.527 --> 01:06:04.197
<i>- Hopeless.
- Is he hurt?</i>


01:06:05.330 --> 01:06:07.730
<i> I have to say yes</i>


01:06:08.232 --> 01:06:09.572
<i> and no to that.</i>


01:06:11.035 --> 01:06:12.265
<i> We are beaten.</i>


01:06:13.136 --> 01:06:15.906
<i>Andy does not break.</i>


01:06:16.339 --> 01:06:17.879
<i> Ever.</i>


01:06:17.908 --> 01:06:20.948
<i>Never complain, never show fear.</i>


01:06:22.046 --> 01:06:23.176
<i>Always hope.</i>


01:06:24.714 --> 01:06:27.814
How did you see him? Were you
in the same cell together?


01:06:32.288 --> 01:06:33.588
<i>Uh...</i>


01:06:35.291 --> 01:06:36.701
<i>They move us.</i>


01:06:37.126 --> 01:06:39.025
<i>But, um...</i>


01:06:39.060 --> 01:06:41.870
<i>Always the foreigners
are in one room,</i>


01:06:41.897 --> 01:06:44.237
<i>and the Arabs in other rooms.</i>


01:06:45.800 --> 01:06:47.741
<i>Much better for us
in a way because...</i>


01:06:50.472 --> 01:06:53.041
<i>They have no limits
with the Arabic prisoners.</i>


01:06:53.941 --> 01:06:58.011
<i>With us they kick, they punch,</i>


01:06:59.779 --> 01:07:01.390
<i>but there's no clamp with us,</i>


01:07:01.415 --> 01:07:03.985
<i>no car battery...</i>


01:07:07.987 --> 01:07:10.627
<i>It is a kind of torture
to listen to torture.</i>


01:07:13.425 --> 01:07:14.766
<i>But Andy</i>


01:07:15.328 --> 01:07:16.838
<i>is always reminding us</i>


01:07:18.432 --> 01:07:20.031
<i>we are protected more,</i>


01:07:20.065 --> 01:07:23.205
<i>we have value,
because we are foreigners.</i>


01:07:25.604 --> 01:07:27.303
Well, Andy's gift
has always been


01:07:27.338 --> 01:07:30.309
to be able to see the bright
spot in the crappiest situation.


01:07:32.311 --> 01:07:34.610
<i>Andy never loses hope, Helen.</i>


01:07:35.412 --> 01:07:36.682
<i>Every day,</i>


01:07:38.115 --> 01:07:39.554
<i>he kneels</i>


01:07:39.582 --> 01:07:41.622
<i>and says a little
morning prayer,</i>


01:07:42.253 --> 01:07:43.653
<i>quiet to himself.</i>


01:07:44.555 --> 01:07:45.855
<i>Then he rolls the bed up,</i>


01:07:46.657 --> 01:07:48.157
<i>makes a space to sit,</i>


01:07:49.125 --> 01:07:51.235
<i>very clean and tidy.</i>


01:07:52.195 --> 01:07:55.834
<i>While the rest of us,
we just leave the mats.</i>


01:07:56.633 --> 01:07:58.373
<i>But Andy</i>


01:07:58.401 --> 01:08:00.370
<i>starts the morning like this,</i>


01:08:00.403 --> 01:08:03.573
<i>every morning since he arrived.</i>


01:08:03.606 --> 01:08:07.076
<i>So eventually, we all
start folding the mats, too.</i>


01:08:09.944 --> 01:08:11.489
Well, that must have
started over there,


01:08:11.513 --> 01:08:15.222
because you should see the
way his room looks at home.


01:08:16.951 --> 01:08:19.621
That's what I'm going to do.
As soon as I get him back,


01:08:19.654 --> 01:08:21.863
I'm going to make him
clean up all his shit.


01:08:22.656 --> 01:08:24.527
<i>You will see him again, Helen.</i>


01:08:24.559 --> 01:08:26.559
<i>He is going to make it.</i>


01:08:26.594 --> 01:08:28.533
<i>They paid the money
to release me</i>


01:08:28.562 --> 01:08:29.872
<i>and Andy</i>


01:08:30.664 --> 01:08:32.394
<i>is worth 100 of me.</i>


01:10:38.449 --> 01:10:40.218
Hey.
What can I get you?


01:10:40.250 --> 01:10:41.390
I'm fine.


01:10:41.418 --> 01:10:42.618
- You sure?
- Yeah, I'm good.


01:10:42.653 --> 01:10:43.963
Oh.


01:10:43.987 --> 01:10:46.827
So, congratulations.


01:10:47.558 --> 01:10:48.988
On the proof of life.


01:10:49.793 --> 01:10:51.163
That was days ago.


01:10:51.194 --> 01:10:53.793
Andy is alive.
There's still hope.


01:10:53.829 --> 01:10:56.069
Can I ask you something?
A-L-M.


01:10:56.098 --> 01:10:58.468
Your proof of life question.


01:10:58.500 --> 01:10:59.700
What was carved into the tree.


01:10:59.736 --> 01:11:01.506
What does A-L-M stand for?


01:11:02.405 --> 01:11:04.275
Greta Remelli.


01:11:04.307 --> 01:11:06.177
Vanessa Marzullo.
Do you know them?


01:11:06.208 --> 01:11:08.047
- I...
- Or Nicholas Henin.


01:11:08.076 --> 01:11:10.916
Pierre Torres.
Edouard Elias.


01:11:11.412 --> 01:11:12.542
Loic Dejan.


01:11:13.481 --> 01:11:14.691
Are they friends of Andy's?


01:11:14.716 --> 01:11:17.016
No. They're hostages.


01:11:17.052 --> 01:11:19.412
They were hostages.
They're home now.


01:11:20.854 --> 01:11:22.454
You know why they're home.


01:11:22.489 --> 01:11:23.729
I know why they're home.


01:11:23.757 --> 01:11:25.427
They're home because
their governments...


01:11:25.459 --> 01:11:28.129
- Helen, we've talked...
- Do not interrupt me, please.


01:11:30.030 --> 01:11:33.070
They're home because their
governments paid the ransom.


01:11:35.234 --> 01:11:37.004
Did you think if we met
outside the office


01:11:37.037 --> 01:11:39.107
I'd have something different
to tell you about this?


01:11:39.138 --> 01:11:42.078
Will you talk to me like a
human being for once, Eric?


01:11:42.108 --> 01:11:43.378
Helen,


01:11:43.410 --> 01:11:45.870
you know what happens once
we pay out one ransom?


01:11:45.911 --> 01:11:47.441
We create a market.


01:11:47.480 --> 01:11:50.949
American lives gain a very
public monetary value,


01:11:50.982 --> 01:11:53.252
and that value
increases over time.


01:11:53.285 --> 01:11:55.025
It stops becoming political.


01:11:55.053 --> 01:11:57.953
It starts becoming a business.


01:11:57.989 --> 01:12:01.019
These guys call themselves
the Islamic State


01:12:01.060 --> 01:12:02.059
or the New Caliphate,


01:12:02.092 --> 01:12:04.192
or whatever name will
sound badass


01:12:04.228 --> 01:12:06.658
to some angry 16-year-old
on Twitter.


01:12:06.697 --> 01:12:07.774
But they're really
just the mafia.


01:12:07.798 --> 01:12:09.458
But the French pay.


01:12:09.500 --> 01:12:11.100
The Italians pay.


01:12:12.737 --> 01:12:14.777
Not a single European government


01:12:14.805 --> 01:12:16.204
has admitted to paying a ransom


01:12:16.239 --> 01:12:17.669
to a terrorist organization.


01:12:17.707 --> 01:12:20.207
Well, they don't shout it from
the rooftops, but they pay


01:12:20.243 --> 01:12:22.212
and you know damn well they pay.


01:12:22.244 --> 01:12:25.585
I don't. I don't know who's
been telling you that,


01:12:25.615 --> 01:12:28.385
but I have no idea how
they got them out of there.


01:12:31.653 --> 01:12:32.653
Right.


01:12:38.327 --> 01:12:39.987
Payment made to
a terrorist organization


01:12:40.028 --> 01:12:42.258
is illegal. I need
to reiterate that.


01:12:42.297 --> 01:12:45.226
Do you think that
at this point in my life,


01:12:45.266 --> 01:12:48.096
I'm afraid of a jail sentence?


01:12:48.136 --> 01:12:49.935
Not just you, Helen.


01:12:49.970 --> 01:12:51.741
Anyone and everyone


01:12:51.773 --> 01:12:54.143
who assists you in any way.


01:12:54.942 --> 01:12:56.382
You'll send them to jail, too.


01:13:14.260 --> 01:13:17.100
Do you send any of your
paycheck home to Iran?


01:13:20.232 --> 01:13:23.772
No. It's difficult
with the sanctions.


01:13:23.803 --> 01:13:25.002
Oh.


01:13:32.109 --> 01:13:34.250
Is Christmas important
in your family?


01:13:35.113 --> 01:13:36.943
Was when my kid was little.


01:13:40.617 --> 01:13:41.957
Do you have kids?


01:13:42.553 --> 01:13:44.523
No.


01:13:44.555 --> 01:13:45.954
No. But seven sisters.


01:13:45.989 --> 01:13:47.300
Oh, God.


01:13:47.324 --> 01:13:50.464
Oh, that explains so much.


01:13:54.664 --> 01:13:56.594
Ah. You know,


01:13:57.099 --> 01:13:58.539
I miss the noise,


01:13:59.368 --> 01:14:00.608
the gatherings,


01:14:01.471 --> 01:14:02.531
the food. Oh!


01:14:05.840 --> 01:14:09.670
You know the hardest thing to
get used to, coming to America,


01:14:11.046 --> 01:14:12.346
is the silence.


01:14:15.450 --> 01:14:16.480
Hmm.


01:14:19.187 --> 01:14:20.556
You must miss your son.


01:14:24.291 --> 01:14:25.291
I do.


01:14:26.292 --> 01:14:28.062
He's a journalist, right?


01:14:28.461 --> 01:14:29.592
Yes, he is.


01:14:30.631 --> 01:14:31.761
Where is he now?


